A||N||9||2xsess||Tranny Question||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||09-26-2000||06:02 PM||||I'm thinking of putting an 87Gt 5spd in my 85GT 4spd. What do I need to do to complete this? Do I need the shifter cables and/or the flywheel?<P>Also, what clutch would I buy to put in, 87 or 85?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||09-26-2000||06:14 PM||||Also, my 4spd right now is giving me trouble, when I'm moving it shifts fine but, when I'm at a stop or just barely moving it doesn't want to come out of or go into gear. Is this a symptom of clutch or slave cylinder malfunction?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||09-26-2000||08:33 PM||||HELP PLEASE!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||09-26-2000||08:51 PM||||That sounds like a clutch prob to me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||09-27-2000||08:01 AM||||Do I have to drop the cradle to replace the clutch. I thought I read a thread where someone said that you could do it with cradle in.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||09-27-2000||09:10 AM||||When you shift while moving do you have to match the engine rpms to the trans rpms or will it shift at any engine rpm?  If you have to match the rpms then it sounds like the clutch is not disengaging.  <P>While moving you don't actually need the clutch to switch between forward gears.  All you have to do is match the rpms between the input and output shafts and gears will change.<P>I saw a write-up about changing the clutch without removing the engine or trans from the car and without dropping the cradle.  Personally I'd drop the cradle.  It's not as hard as it seems.  Of course my thoughts on that have changed a lot from before I dropped my cradle to now.<P>With the cradle out you have access to lots of things not easily reachable with the engine in the car.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000006||2xsess||09-27-2000||11:45 AM||||No I don't have to match the RPMs at all, as long as I'm moving and press the clutch in it shifts fine. <P>Thanks Carrolles<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||Terrible Tom||09-27-2000||11:56 AM||||Check your clutch hydrolics first.  I had a similar problem and had someone depress the clutch while I was looking at the slave cylinder.  The slave ram went forward and then slowly started to return by itself.  Turns out it was a bad master cylinder and an easy fix.  Of course, I didn't check this until I had already changed the clutch, but that's another story.||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||09-27-2000||12:02 PM||||I was just reading something about that at Rodneys website, thanks Tom <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
